PART 1: The buff-sandstone Georgian/Victorian tenements with bay windows, plus the "Funeralcare" (Co-op) shop sign, point strongly to Scotland, and the craggy flat-topped hill dead ahead looks like Arthur's Seat/Salisbury Crags, making Edinburgh near-certain. Left-hand traffic, UK road signs and bollards confirm Britain. The vista down a wide tenement street toward the Crags best matches Easter Road looking south toward the London Road junction.

