PART 1: The red-brick townhouses with tall white louvered shutters and stone trim are classic northern French (Picardy/Nord) architecture, and driving is on the right with French-style bike lane markings, green communal waste bins, and a modern French street lamp. The ornate stone corner building with carved inscription and arched carriage entrance suggests a prosperous mid-sized city like Amiens rather than Lille. The wide boulevard layout and车辆 models (Renault/Peugeot era cars) fit a French regional capital. Everything points to Amiens in the Somme, Hauts-de-France.

