PART 1: The dry ichu grass, rounded barren hills, and extremely high-altitude altiplano scenery point straight to the Andean plateau of Bolivia or southern Peru. The unfinished exposed-brick buildings with painted trim, concrete utility poles, yellow centerline with white edge lines, and right-hand driving are classic Bolivian altiplano road style (Ruta 1 between La Paz and Oruro). The green highway sign and telecom towers on the hill ahead suggest approaching a small town along that corridor, and the brick architecture leans more Bolivia than Puno, Peru.

